ized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Retrieval of Shared Verifiable Presentation using Access Token\nDescription: Verifiers can now retry the retrieval of a shared verifiable presentation using a valid access token multiple times until the token expires, rather than a single retrieval attempt as before.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: 3.12\n\n--- Record 325 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Mandatory email for job subscribers\nDescription: A message in the UI now ensures that all subscribers for job notifications provide an email address.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 326 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Try out GraphQL Queries in the Graph Navigator on the Developer Hub\nDescription: You can try out GraphQL queries in the Graph Navigator on the Developer Hub. For more information, see Graph Navigator on Developer Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-11\nValid as Of: 2025-08-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 327 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.20.2\nDescription: Version 1.20.2 introduces the following improvements:      The Istio module now supports the use of Istio sidecars as Kubernetes init containers. In addition to the default Istio containers, the module also restarts native sidecar init containers. However, configuring native sidecars directly from the Istio Custom Resource (CR) is not supported. For more information, see issue #1426.Caution  If your cluster's Istio service mesh includes workloads with initContainer sidecars, the Istio module will restart these workloads for the first time. See Restart of Workloads with Enabled Istio Sidecar Injection, Istio sidecar documentation, and Kubernetes Native Sidecars in Istio.    We've updated the Istio version to 1.26.2. For more information, read the Istio 1.26.2 release announcement and Istio 1.26.0 release announcement.  We've fixed a bug where the proxy-protocol EnvoyFilter applied by the Istio module on AWS clusters with ELB load balancers was incorrectly detected as a user resource. This resulted in the Istio custom resource being set to the Warning state. See issue #1491.  We've fixed a bug where labels of the Istio managed resources were not correctly reconciled.  We've fixed a bug where the app.kubernetes.io/version label was not set to the proper version in the managed resources.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-22\nValid as Of: 2025-08-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 328 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration of SAP Document AI (Embedded Edition) with SAP Mobile Start\nDescription: You can now integrate SAP Document AI with SAP Mobile Start. The integration lets you use your mobile device to upload documents or scan printed documents and then upload the resulting images for automatic information extraction.  See Integrating SAP Document AI With Your SAP Solution (Embedded Edition and Premium Edition).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-04\nValid as Of: 2025-08-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 329 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: ELSTER Adapter Supports New ERiC Version\nDescription: A new version 42.2.2.0 of the Elster Rich Client (ERiC) library is available for the ELSTER adapter.   This update includes enhanced data type versions\",287\n212,\" Cloud Integration using the pipeline approach.  See: Pipeline Approach and Migration Approaches.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-06\nValid as Of: 2025-04-06\nVersion: 2502\n\n--- Record 1090 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Modifying Externalized Parameter descriptions in Integration Flow\nDescription:  You can now modify the information about the parameter from the Externalized Parameters view.  For more information, see Externalized Parameters View  SAP Cloud Integration customers, see Externalized Parameters View\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-06\nValid as Of: 2025-04-06\nVersion: 2502\n\n\",272\n346,\"--- Record 1061 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Operator \"\"Exists\"\" for Company Policies\nDescription: When you create rules for company policies, you can now use the operator exists in combination with the attribute contract reference. Create a new rule, select the attribute contract reference, then select exists. The value of the rule is left empty on purpose to define that the company policy should check if any contract reference exists in the provider's offer.  See Create and Edit Company Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: 2502\n\n--- Record 1062 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.7.*      Increment: 2502      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLa